  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p>The Sporting Blaster Carbine is designed to take the compact design of the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Blaster_Carbine\" title=\"Blaster Carbine\">Blaster Carbine</a> and increase its accuracy, making it more competitive at long ranges. The bounty hunter Jariah Syn uses a Sporting Blaster Carbine on occasion. </p><p>A Sporting Blaster Carbine is not treated as an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Inaccurate\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Inaccurate\">Inaccurate</a> Weapon when wielded in two hands. Sporting Blaster Carbines have&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Retractable_Stocks\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Retractable Stocks\">Retractable Stocks</a>. Like all carbines, the Sporting Blaster Carbine can be used to make&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Attacks_of_Opportunity\" title=\"Attacks of Opportunity\">Attacks of Opportunity</a>, even without a folded stock. </p><p>A Sporting Blaster Carbine requires a&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a>&nbsp;to operate. After 100 shots, the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a>&nbsp;must be replaced. </p><p><b>Inaccurate:</b>&nbsp;This weapon cannot fire at targets at Long&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p>",
